    verification setJudgmentWritePathRefineGate : Test { :>> id = "1a26e7ec-0ce6-4a9f-8102-2fe435d25398"; :>> title = "Sprint 668 refine gate (DoR)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-11"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Chartered by D0443 (proposed, process-change: a new write verb, a new policy key and two census rows, so the commit carries the marked Decision and the human's word accepts it; NOT A FORK - D0312 B chose the shape). Sized 5 points: a new verb across twelve files (attestation, write, main, deck, serve, census, control_structure, activation, cli_facts, cli_surface, commands.sysml, the policy) with a unit pair, a write test pair and a three-case integration test. Read before design: write.rs accept_decision_locked and refuse_ai_judgment are the channel; main.rs verdict_channel_refusal was hard-wired to decisionAcceptance and the read-back WARN, so it takes the delegation class and a read-back flag; attestation.rs proposed_count was the only reader of VerdictKind::proposed; deck.rs collect had two card classes; serve.rs KEEL_API_WRITE_ENDPOINTS is the census's list of write endpoints. FINDING 4 of sprint 663's retro (D0049 autonomy vs D0312 B proposed) resolves here by cost: the human judges one sampled set per file, not one item per gate. DoR: points set, charter edge set, DoD authored, dcProposedOutcomeTier done."; }
